{"name":"September Aster","hex":"#a8bedd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants of the genus Aster; one of its flowers.","A star-shaped structure formed during the mitosis of a cell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aster (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"Aster is a genus of perennial flowering plants in the family Asteraceae. Its circumscription has been narrowed, and it now encompasses around 170 species, all but one of which are restricted to Eurasia; many species formerly in Aster are now in other genera of the tribe Astereae. Aster amellus is the type species of the genus and the family Asteraceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG/330px-Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_(genus)"},{"title":"Aster (missile family)","blocks":[{"text":"The Aster 15 and Aster 30 are a Franco-Italian family of all-weather, vertical launch surface-to-air missiles. The name \"Aster\" stands for \"Aérospatiale Terminale\", with French company Aérospatiale having been the project's lead contractor before its missile activities were merged into MBDA. It also takes inspiration from the word \"aster\", meaning \"star\" in Ancient Greek. The missiles as well as the related weapon systems are manufactured by Eurosam, a consortium consisting of MBDA France, MBDA Italy and Thales, each holding a 33.3% share."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/MBDA_Aster_p1220947.jpg/330px-MBDA_Aster_p1220947.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_(missile_family)"},{"title":"September","blocks":[{"text":"September is the ninth month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 30 days."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_septembre.jpg/330px-Les_Tr%C3%A8s_Riches_Heures_du_duc_de_Berry_septembre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/September"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/500px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/1280px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/500px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Multi layer petals Aster flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAster_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Aster-alpinus.JPG/500px-Aster-alpinus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Aster-alpinus.JPG/500px-Aster-alpinus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aster alpinus is the only species of Aster (sensu stricto) that is native to North America; it is found in mountains across the Northern Hemisphere.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAster-alpinus.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Type_45_HMS_Diamond_being_loaded_with_Sea_Viper_missiles_at_HMNB_Portsmouth_MOD_45159617.jpg/500px-Type_45_HMS_Diamond_being_loaded_with_Sea_Viper_missiles_at_HMNB_Portsmouth_MOD_45159617.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Type_45_HMS_Diamond_being_loaded_with_Sea_Viper_missiles_at_HMN